#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:16
msgid ""
"They **add up** rather than exclude one another, and mixing them is the "
"normal case — structured extraction with unstructured filtering, say. "
"Merging happens by summing the **same-named** pipelines of the three "
"levels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:20
msgid ""
"Start at the most constrained level that works and drop down only where "
"you must. A report whose investment table is perfectly ordinary may still"
" name its funds in a way nothing can parameterise; inheriting two "
"segments and writing the third is what keeps a hard format from costing "
"three times a simple one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:25
msgid "1. Declare the format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:27
msgid ""
"Add a row to `metadata/formats.csv`, by **components** rather than by "
"name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:34
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The name every other file refers to — `CARNE-EN23` — is synthesised as "
"`Name-Locale<YY>[@Country][.Version]` and written nowhere else, so a name"
" and its components cannot disagree. See {doc}`repository`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:38
msgid ""
"If the reports come from a stable address, add a prefix to "
"`metadata/url_mapping.csv` so the format is inferred without `--format`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:41
msgid "2. Put the report and the test companies in place"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:47
msgid "and, once per repository, `freeports-dev setup-input-db`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:49
msgid "3. Find out which pages matter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:55
msgid ""
"Nothing is classified yet, so everything comes back `unclassified` — that"
" is the starting point, not a failure. Open the PDF, find a page of the "
"table you want, and note what makes it recognisable: a header, a font, a "
"phrase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:59
msgid "4. Classify"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:61
msgid ""
"Write the classification rows or pipe, then run `inspect-document` again "
"until the right pages carry the right class. At the structured level this"
" is two or three rows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:70
msgid ""
"Rows sharing an id describe **one** pipe, and a page belongs to the class"
" if it contains **all** of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:73
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Do not go further until this is right.** Chasing the extraction of a "
"page the engine never selected is the single most common way to lose an "
"afternoon ({doc}`../../reference/design/classification`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:77
msgid "5. Schedule the class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:79
msgid ""
"A class no step mentions is an **error**, so add it to "
"`content/orchestration/algorithms_schedule.csv`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:86
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Raise `Filter next iteration` on the last class of a step when what that "
"step finds should filter the next one "
"({doc}`../../reference/design/schedule`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:89
msgid "6. Extract, one segment at a time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:97
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In that order. Each mode shows what one segment made of the page, so a "
"wrong result tells you **which segment** is wrong rather than that the "
"page is wrong. {doc}`dev-loop`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:100
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Most of what you write here is a **selection** — a predicate over the "
"lines of a page. {doc}`selections`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:103
msgid "7. Freeze it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:109
msgid ""
"Three JSON fixtures for that page, one per segment. Read what it prints "
"before confirming: `make-tests` records *what the code does now*, so "
"confirming a wrong result promotes a bug into the specification and the "
"test will then defend it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:113
msgid ""
"Repeat for a handful of representative pages — the first page of a table,"
" a continuation page, a page with an awkward row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:116
msgid "8. Run the whole document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:122
msgid ""
"The per-page tests are fast. The whole-document test compares the output "
"tables against `tests/formats/CARNE-EN23/out/`, and the first time there "
"is nothing to compare against: generate it deliberately, **after reading "
"it**, because from then on it is the format's specification and not a "
"snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:127
msgid "9. Vouch for it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:129
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The reference output of a format is a claim about the world. The project "
"records who is making it and on what basis — {doc}`../../overview/trust` "
"for the mechanism, {doc}`../../reference/cli/index` for the commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:132
msgid "Two rules about matching and unresolved pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:133
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Company matching is first-match-wins, in file order.** The input "
"database's order is meaningful, not incidental. A format that seems to "
"attribute a holding to the wrong company is often reporting a database "
"problem rather than an extraction one. See {doc}`../input-db/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/writing-a-format.md:137
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A page that cannot fully resolve is not a failed page.** Reach for a "
"promise before reaching for a second pass. If the fund name is on the "
"cover and the table is on page 412, the table *promises* the name and the"
" cover supplies it. Adding an ordering constraint between pages instead "
"gives up everything the page-as-unit assumption buys "
"({doc}`../../reference/design/promises`)."
msgstr ""

